{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder","id":1078931,"title":"[2E] How possible is domain ruled by truly Elder?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-15T09:46:35-07:00","id":1078931,"title":"[2E] How possible is domain ruled by truly Elder?","content":"I'm preparing modern day Swedish <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uppsala\" target=\"_blank\">Uppsala</a> setting, for my <b>Werewolf </b>game. As I envisioned that Kindred are larger force in Scandinavia on general, I think about repercussions the local Archbishop ( Prince - Bishop ) of Lancea et Sanctum could have on region. I envisioned him to be literal 'mortal dead, vampire risen' one of most controversial of real world Lutheran Bishops of Uppsala region - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham_Angermannus\" target=\"_blank\">Abraham Angermannus</a> - that was famous for starting local 'witch trials'. In my version, Abraham at his death bed was Embraced by the Deava 'succubus' and send back to Uppsala to 'make order with heresies'. He was so good, he become de facto local Prince, even if still wanting to be called Archbishop.<br /> <br /> Thing is, in modern nights, he will be over 400 years old. <b>Is it possible in 2E game to have Elder as old an active Archbishop/Prince? </b>Or should I look for someone lot younger, like up to 200 years? How much Blood Potency will be problem for long running the same office in Kindred society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:44:05-07:00","id":1079054,"title":"","content":"I think it is certainly possible. I believe there is a Theban ritual or two that can help with the Vinculum, and a prince could collect a blood tax on those in his domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:50:55-07:00","id":1079059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder#post1078931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, in modern nights, he will be over 400 years old. <b>Is it possible in 2E game to have Elder as old an active Archbishop/Prince? </b>Or should I look for someone lot younger, like up to 200 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much Blood Potency will be problem for long running the same office in Kindred society? </div> </div> </div>You might have some trouble with 1-2 Blood Potency but they could be propped up by a powerful backer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:59:59-07:00","id":1079065,"title":"","content":"Aye, there are many ways. In addition to mystical ways of avoiding Vinculum, a Prince could Pervert themselves with a trusted compatriot to avoid later Vinculum. <br /> <br /> You can also be an elder without having high BP. You don't have to drink pure Vitae until you're approximately 300 years old. But Blood Potency over years is a guideline, it's fully possible for him to not reach that point for 500 or 600 years. Additionally, if he spends over 25 years (again, roughly) in Torpor, he loses a BP. 25 years is nothing. Perhaps there was a hiccup in his life, and sometime in, say, the 1800s, he fell into torpor for 50 to 75 years. That'd put him even using a strict 50-year-per-BP rule, under the restriction for BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:07:57-07:00","id":1079190,"title":"","content":"There's also the option of sleeping off Blood Potency from time to time, and having a trusted Herald rule while he is in Torpor. Or even better, if the Herald has the Speaker for the Silent Merit, he can literally rule through his Herald while he slumbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T08:52:30-07:00","id":1079383,"title":"","content":"There is no need for Preversion. Here's a rhetorical question, why wouldn't a sire 400 years ago, before the era of the modern notions freedom and autonomy, NOT blood bond thier childer? <br /> <br /> Receiving a shipment from his sire that includes a Reliquaries created by his sire each month keeps the stage 3 bond, possible keep enough Vitae to rise each night, and the bond allow the Archbishop Prince to feed via a Vitae tithe to supplement his need to use the abilities granted by the blood.<br /> <br /> Who says a Prince can't be beholden to outside powers?<br /> <br /> Honestly most vampires embraced by someone who has pre-French revoltion notions should be bound to thier sire, and even those more modern should have a large percentage bound, it just is very tempting for potential sires and justifiable as a form of protection, if you don't bind them then someone who cares less than you do for them will one day...<br /> <br /> Also let's not forget the religious concept of the Chain of Being which makes the Invictus and Lance understand each other so well. Sires should be above childer, it just makes sense and unlike parental relationship which are driven to change by biological and neurological development, vampires are normally embraced after such changes and are fairly static beings, which adds stability to such relationships, especially if the childer don't have to live in thier sire's house under thier rules, so to speak.<br /> <br /> This of course raises the question, how does the sire get Vitae being so ancient. By being a vassel in an Invictus city of course! First and second estates indeed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 04-16-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:03:32-07:00","id":1079417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079383#post1079383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no need for Preversion. Here's a rhetorical question, why wouldn't a sire 400 years ago, before the era of the modern notions freedom and autonomy, NOT blood bond thier childer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but if Mother of Archbishop Prince is one of this 'Dark Succubus' Deava, what does it mean? I would suspect she would be much quicker on Final Death, as she:<br /> 1. Was much older to begin with ( probably Embraced in late Middle Ages ).<br /> 2. As 'Dark Succubus' she travels - a lot. And travel means danger for Kindred. When Archbishop Prince is more or less in the same domain all the time.<br /> <br /> So logical his 'Mother' would be dead quicker than him. I even imagined her dying circa French Revolution, when she was trying to push peasants in to 'Church affraid', but was dealt by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079383#post1079383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Receiving a shipment from his sire that includes a Reliquaries created by his sire each month keeps the stage 3 bond, possible keep enough Vitae to rise each night, and the bond allow the Archbishop Prince to feed via a Vitae tithe to supplement his need to use the abilities granted by the blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I have only pass by knowledge of <b>Requiem</b> line - <b>What are Reliquaries and where can I read more on them?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079383#post1079383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also let's not forget the religious concept of the Chain of Being which makes the Invictus and Lance understand each other so well. Sires should be above childer, it just makes sense and unlike parental relationship which are driven to change by biological and neurological development, vampires are normally embraced after such changes and are fairly static beings, which adds stability to such relationships, especially if the childer don't have to live in thier sire's house under thier rules, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_chain_of_being\" target=\"_blank\">Chain of Being</a>, I must say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079383#post1079383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This of course raises the question, how does the sire get Vitae being so ancient. By being a vassel in an Invictus city of course! First and second estates indeed...</div> </div> </div> </div>What Vassel to Invictus? Archbishop is highest Lancea et Sanctum in region. It's more like Invictus need to answer to him - or rather try to work with him and not make him angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:42:43-07:00","id":1079451,"title":"","content":"Vitae Reliquary is a low level Theban Sorcery ritual which allows the caster to store a few points of vitae in an object. So a Theban sorceror could place 4 vitae into a book or piece of jewelry etc. mail it to another vampire and that vampire can take the vitae stored in the object. It wouldn't need to be a superior doing it either. This hypothetical bishop could have lower ranked Sanctified sorcerers tithing him as well as part of their clerical duties. (If he's in vinculum to someone else, it's not a risk anymore.)<br /> <br /> And being the vassal in an Invictus oath is simply to designate who gets what out of the oath, not the actual city position. He could have Invictus status 3, get an Invictus status 1 character (whom he awards tenurial privileges to) to act as liege in an oath of fealty and take 3 vitae a week from his &quot;liege&quot;. Or have 1 Invictus status and place the Oath of Serfdom on anyone to whom he subinfeudates territory and gets blood tithes from them or just feed off them directly since he's immune to blood bonds from them.<br /> Or with Invictus 1 status, use the Oath of Penance on anyone who's breached his rules to collect every 10th vitae from violators for a duration set by the oath.<br /> Technically there is no notarized violation since the liege IS an Invictus member, even though he is the leader of another covenant entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":".  spelling errors 04-16-2017, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:43:17-07:00","id":1079663,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a>, I will probably go with Reliquary idea - bloody <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacramental_bread\" target=\"_blank\">hostia</a> and all that. When running Lance domian, go all the way in to it, right? <i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:09:35-07:00","id":1079822,"title":"","content":"Reliquary is always a good idea as it's a very handy ritual (the only limitation is it has an expiration date, but you could imagine a higher ranked ritual where that limitation doesn't exist). Even then, 50 years per BP dot is only a guideline. Like it's been said, holding off on human blood, not using disciplines too much could very well hold that back (how much is your own choice). Given that he's risen to power quickly and held it for long, though, I'd imagine he wasn't the type to hold back when he needed to.<br /> <br /> Plus, yes, a few decades of naptime is a good way to wind the clock back a little, especially since there is no more fog of time (where your memory became muddy when you experienced torpor in 1e), so the only limit to it is making sure people won't turn on you too much in the meantime so you can go back into office easily when you wake up. 50 years isn't that much for a 250 years old vampire, but lots can happen in that time. Any prince who can go to sleep and then quickly come back into power when they wake up are bound to be respected by other vampires.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I don't think 400 years is too old for a prince. There's no such thing as too old and while 2e doesn't present any kindred that old holding that title (1e had a few vampires who were much older, though), it states nowhere that it's impossible. My guess is part of the point is to not make super old broken NPCs as a restrictive metaplot and instead have GMs come up with their own (ald also the &quot;personal horror&quot; thing which is more street level than ancient tyrants), so I wouldn't let myself be intimidated by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:00:35-07:00","id":1080029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079822#post1079822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reliquary is always a good idea as it's a very handy ritual (the only limitation is it has an expiration date, but you could imagine a higher ranked ritual where that limitation doesn't exist). Even then, 50 years per BP dot is only a guideline. Like it's been said, holding off on human blood, not using disciplines too much could very well hold that back (how much is your own choice). Given that he's risen to power quickly and held it for long, though, I'd imagine he wasn't the type to hold back when he needed to.<br /> <br /> Plus, yes, a few decades of naptime is a good way to wind the clock back a little, especially since there is no more fog of time (where your memory became muddy when you experienced torpor in 1e), so the only limit to it is making sure people won't turn on you too much in the meantime so you can go back into office easily when you wake up. 50 years isn't that much for a 250 years old vampire, but lots can happen in that time. Any prince who can go to sleep and then quickly come back into power when they wake up are bound to be respected by other vampires.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I don't think 400 years is too old for a prince. There's no such thing as too old and while 2e doesn't present any kindred that old holding that title (1e had a few vampires who were much older, though), it states nowhere that it's impossible. My guess is part of the point is to not make super old broken NPCs as a restrictive metaplot and instead have GMs come up with their own (ald also the &quot;personal horror&quot; thing which is more street level than ancient tyrants), so I wouldn't let myself be intimidated by that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the whole idea with the reliquary is great in general, but the expiration date isn't the only limitation. I don't have any books atm to check, but if I can remember the reliquary blood can make blood bonds, so there is always a risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T00:58:45-07:00","id":1080209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1080029#post1080029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the whole idea with the reliquary is great in general, but the expiration date isn't the only limitation. I don't have any books atm to check, but if I can remember the reliquary blood can make blood bonds, so there is always a risk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. Blood stored in reliquary can still cause vinculum and for all purposes acts as if it was drank straight from someones vein. <br /> <br /> Also am I the only one that finds it hilarious that LS allows you to build vampire paladin chugging health/mana potions in combat and slinging holy magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T01:05:23-07:00","id":1080212,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, that's right. Man, that ritual suffered the transition to 2e. The 1e version lasted forever and made the blood neutral in terms of vinculum (and used to be level 1 too). Maybe they wanted to avoid a hack where elders could just have underlings mail them reliquaries to bypass the blood restrictions, or maybe it seemed wrong that a low level power like that could circumvent vinculum, which are supposed to be a pretty big deal and not that easy to avoid ? Still doesn't seam that unbalanced considering an invictus oath can have a similar result. Now, it's basically a way to make glorified flasks of blood to take to parties when you don't want to spend money at the bar.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the easy solution is to make a higher level ritual, again, or a devotion to eliminate the vinculum part. The Archbishop will want to make damn sure he'll be present every time this ritual is made to be sure it's not the normal version.<br /> <br /> There have to be more subtle ways, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:42:25-07:00","id":1080350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1080212#post1080212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, that's right. Man, that ritual suffered the transition to 2e. The 1e version lasted forever and made the blood neutral in terms of vinculum (and used to be level 1 too). Maybe they wanted to avoid a hack where elders could just have underlings mail them reliquaries to bypass the blood restrictions, or maybe it seemed wrong that a low level power like that could circumvent vinculum, which are supposed to be a pretty big deal and not that easy to avoid ? Still doesn't seam that unbalanced considering an invictus oath can have a similar result. Now, it's basically a way to make glorified flasks of blood to take to parties when you don't want to spend money at the bar.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the easy solution is to make a higher level ritual, again, or a devotion to eliminate the vinculum part. The Archbishop will want to make damn sure he'll be present every time this ritual is made to be sure it's not the normal version.<br /> <br /> There have to be more subtle ways, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup the 1st edition Vitae Reliquary was unbalanced. If I remember correctly you could use an item size of an apple which won't rot, for example a tennis ball and make yourself &quot;potions&quot; like in DnD. Even sell them like a gnome mage. I'm sure every ST would &quot;reward&quot; such dedicated Theban sorcery user, but nevertheless it was possible. Current version is much better IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:09:25-07:00","id":1080434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079383#post1079383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no need for Preversion. Here's a rhetorical question, why wouldn't a sire 400 years ago, before the era of the modern notions freedom and autonomy, NOT blood bond thier childer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disapproval of slavery is older than 400 years. That said, it's an option.<br /> <br /> But the blood bond instills devotion. It doesn't <i>have to</i> determine which way the power flows. What if the vampire the Bishop is bound to is mad and broken, confined to a cell because he can't survive in the world outside, but protected and cared for by the Bishop because of the bond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:48:21-07:00","id":1080498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079417#post1079417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but if Mother of Archbishop Prince is one of this 'Dark Succubus' Deava, what does it mean? I would suspect she would be much quicker on Final Death, as she:<br /> 1. Was much older to begin with ( probably Embraced in late Middle Ages ).<br /> 2. As 'Dark Succubus' she travels - a lot. And travel means danger for Kindred. When Archbishop Prince is more or less in the same domain all the time</div> </div> </div> </div>The character concept you just described wouldn't need to move around, the second point is a non sequitur. Being a dark succbuss does not require much moving in that era of France&quot;s history, and is indeed quantifying the dark succubus must also be a traveler is inappropriate for such a concept during that time, as travel was uncommon for vampires at that period.<br /> <br /> Lets assume she is competent, politically adept, far from stupid, and thus not dead for simple recklessness. She did embraced a historic figure of some note after all, and that wouldn't be an easy feat to claim such a childer. She'd do quite well to willingly blood bind herself to stable Invictus regimes, who'd be blood bound in turn to his sire or liege. Her not holding blood bonds over those near her is wise as that leads to less resentment over continual control, which would lead some to want to kill her for her interference. Thus keeping her childer far away protects her and them,. While being bound herself is the ultimate seduction, someone willing to be at your mercy, willing to devote themselves to you, can be powerfully motivating for holding the person in great value and prizing them, especially if they are not jealous and don't require you to be exclusive to them.<br /> <br /> Now add daeva level wanton sexy times, powerful political backing, and raw power of an elder vampire, and I'd expect your hypothetical archbishop prince's sire to be doing quite well for herself.<br /> <br /> Invictus have the code for beating the need for blood as Elders, willing blood bonds through fealty chains. Non-Invictus can tap into that, and those bound to those which are have the same benefits but a step removed in the web of loyalty, with Lance sire-childer blood bonds making the ancients able to accepr blood tithes from any member of the Lance et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1079417#post1079417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Vassel to Invictus? Archbishop is highest Lancea et Sanctum in region. It's more like Invictus need to answer to him - or rather try to work with him and not make him angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not talking about the arch bishop, the question that I said was raised was about the arch bishops sire... as above^<br /> <br /> <br /> I realize this is not a simple a to b solution but rather a complex web of interconnected relationships. But it is more plausible than simple answers because it mirrors real life politics and history in complexity.<br /> <br /> Remember: Blood Bonds make you immune to the Blood Bonds of others, they are not something to avoid but to be maintained. Why not be loyal to the person who gave you eternity and plenty of personal space by sending you out as a missionary? Sounds like a sweet deal. Elders are lucky to have blood bond to those they can trust. Who better to trust thank someone who isn't around?<br /> <br /> The old world (in the classic Europe vs Americas sense, not the game lines sense) should have ancient vampires at the top, with only major cleansing events causing renewal (massacres by hunters, infighting, or strix).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1080434#post1080434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disapproval of slavery is older than 400 years. That said, it's an option.<br /> <br /> But the blood bond instills devotion. It doesn't <i>have to</i> determine which way the power flows. What if the vampire the Bishop is bound to is mad and broken, confined to a cell because he can't survive in the world outside, but protected and cared for by the Bishop because of the bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't slavery if you blood bond them and then send them out for missionary work they'd agree to before the embrace and blood bond anyway, in that case the blood bond is a favor protecting them from those that'd use the blood bond to sway them from the cause of the Lance, which given this guy's history he'd be a major advocate for. Also feelings of devotion to someone who only rarely makes a reasonable request and is far away wouldn't be the greatest restriction.<br /> <br /> In your example though, which is valid, I could see the arch bishop prince bound to a vampire that needed restrained for their own well-being taking extreme steps to ease that beings suffering. Keeping them well fed is obvious, if messy for the amount of blood an insane vampire can spend, but also perhaps employing Ordo Dracu in a project in how to cure vampire madness. I see Malkovian Madness plot lines dangling from this premise and perhaps even the root of that plot in the particular world that Chronicle of Darkness takes place. Trying to split separate the madness from a vampire could have all sorts of metaphysical consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 04-19-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T17:18:51-07:00","id":1080651,"title":"","content":"It seems to have been stated here before me, but a Prince could easily (lol easily...) torpor off a bit of BP for a specific period of time that they would be able to ensure their power base wouldn't dwindle with. (the longer the absence, the harder it is to ensure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:25:18-07:00","id":1080815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1080651#post1080651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to have been stated here before me, but a Prince could easily (lol easily...) torpor off a bit of BP for a specific period of time that they would be able to ensure their power base wouldn't dwindle with. (the longer the absence, the harder it is to ensure)</div> </div> </div> </div>Prince's torpor is always a fantastic moment in the Story. Someone could want to assassinate the vampire in Torpor and conquer the domain. The players could defend the Prince or help to defend or assassinate.<br /> Is it really easy torpor of BP? Maybe for some vampires, yes, but those who rule in most of the times need to loose humanity. Hard decisions to make, opponents to kill. There is always someone, who wants to take your place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T13:32:13-07:00","id":1081052,"title":"","content":"I agree about Princely torpor being a momentous thing. A lot can happen in 25 years (Torpor duration to lose 1 BP) and much of it is likely to happen as soon as the Prince falls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:09:20-07:00","id":1081477,"title":"","content":"The prince being that old would have a blood potency around 8 which means he could only feed on humans and animals expending a willpower point per vitae taken. However, he could still feed from vampires only risking the vinculum since he's now immune to vitae addiction. On this front, the first dot of the Protean discipline, Unmarked Grave, provides aide as it allows vitae to feed him without the risk of vinculum. The price would only need to have a couple of subjects do some hunting an bled on his grave an he's good. <br /> <br /> Another thing to consider are invictus oaths, being so old I assume the invictus are present and allies, there would be no conflict with the prince having 1-2 dots of invictus status giving him access to the oaths. The basic merit oaths of Fealty and Penance should provide for a steady diet secure from vinculum. Though he may want to blood bond his apparent &quot;liege&quot; to safely benefit from the Fealty oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:16:40-07:00","id":1082251,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to use Blood Sorcery then there's a Theban rite called the Lord's Chalice. Blood deposited into it and drunk from it doesn't risk a blood bond. An ancient Bishop could easily know the rite. Just have your vassals tithe into the chalice.<br /> <br /> Also if one wants to be a bastard, routinely share drinks with prominent elders. Use Lord's Chalice in most cases but occasionally forget to conduct the rite on a political problem's chalice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T09:54:34-07:00","id":1082295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1082251#post1082251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're willing to use Blood Sorcery then there's a Theban rite called the Lord's Chalice. Blood deposited into it and drunk from it doesn't risk a blood bond. An ancient Bishop could easily know the rite. Just have your vassals tithe into the chalice.<br /> <br /> Also if one wants to be a bastard, routinely share drinks with prominent elders. Use Lord's Chalice in most cases but occasionally forget to conduct the rite on a political problem's chalice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please remind in which book is the Lord's Chalice ritual, because I don't recognize it in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T10:26:40-07:00","id":1082303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?cPath=1_135\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/105095.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?cPath=1_135\" target=\"_blank\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - Onyx Path Publishing | Vampire: The Requiem | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?cPath=1_135\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?cPath=1_135 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - God doesn't love me. But He's given me these teeth&nbsp;to spill your blood and these words to speak over your remains.&nbsp;And </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's actually a later 1E book so you may or may not want to use it. There are parts of it I like more than others but it previewed the nerf to Vitae Reliquary and tossed in the more difficult to use Lord's Chalice. It also intros the idea of vampires with creative thaumaturgy which I could honestly do without but I enjoyed the idea behind threnodies and it had some interesting rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:48:39-07:00","id":1083014,"title":"","content":"Know its another setting, but in a old Vampire Dark ages book it said that a reason not to blood bond your childer was because you want strong childer, not syophantic lackies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T08:30:27-07:00","id":1085464,"title":"","content":"It's also posable that someone has bound them, there's no reason the Dragon who prepares kine so he can hunt them as God intended couldn't have him in thrall and just not care to claim the city as it would take time away from his studys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T04:25:36-07:00","id":1085747,"title":"","content":"Forgot to mention the Oath of Serfdom. By granting territory to a Vassal, the Prince becomes immune to that vassal vinculum and the vassal must also pay a blood rent. Having a couple of these should provide along with an occasional sacramental hunt.<br /> <br /> Again this is an invictus oath so notaries wouldn't normally grant a non-invictus into a Liege position, but if the land is given to the covenant and with him being the prince I think an exception could be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T04:46:44-07:00","id":1085751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basilistik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1078931-2e-how-possible-is-domain-ruled-by-truly-elder?p=1085747#post1085747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot to mention the Oath of Serfdom. By granting territory to a Vassal, the Prince becomes immune to that vassal vinculum and the vassal must also pay a blood rent. Having a couple of these should provide along with an occasional sacramental hunt.<br /> <br /> Again this is an invictus oath so notaries wouldn't normally grant a non-invictus into a Liege position, but if the land is given to the covenant and with him being the prince I think an exception could be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the LS character has covenant status 1 in Invictus, he qualifies as liege for that oath. But from a &quot;realism&quot; perspective, I also find it unlikely that a notary would agree to notarize that oath though unless that bishop was already a vassal to a &quot;real&quot; Invictus member even if <u>that</u> oath isn't publicly known. It does not make sense for a notary to be considered a paragon of Invictus standards if they're busy entrenching other covenants' hegemony and gaining nothing substantial in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T00:11:13-08:00","id":1158102,"title":"","content":"In the topic of Elders from Lancea Sanctum not going Torpor - <b>Thousand Years of Night</b> states Sanctified that goes Torpor are 'blessed' and sought by rest of Covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TYoN, p. 34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The covenant teaches that torpid elder priests receive a sacrament directly from God as they dream, so those who spend time dormant wake to more power and influence than they had before, rather than less. These elders become prophets whose advice shapes the course of the Church\u2019s practices an age at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}